1
00:00:09,271 --> 00:00:10,612
[SPEAKER_00]: How to overcome anxiety?

2
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:21,959
[SPEAKER_01]: That's something everybody... everybody would wonder, at least at some point in their life, but I think probably many people today, it's a... it's quite a... quite a pressing issue.

3
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:32,946
[SPEAKER_01]: The most... the most important thing to realize, at first, is that... well, it's to stop resisting it.

4
00:00:34,087 --> 00:00:35,328
[SPEAKER_01]: You stop trying to get rid of it.

5
00:00:36,188 --> 00:00:37,109
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the necessary

6
00:00:37,802 --> 00:00:38,683
[SPEAKER_01]: necessary steps.

7
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:40,604
[SPEAKER_01]: It's important.

8
00:00:40,684 --> 00:00:43,965
[SPEAKER_01]: It's good that people see anxiety as a problem.

9
00:00:44,206 --> 00:00:51,610
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't just go around ignoring it or trying to forget about it through engaging with sensuality.

10
00:00:51,830 --> 00:01:06,578
[SPEAKER_01]: At the same time, you do have to recognize that the wanting to be free from it, in the long run, is not the same as trying to get rid of it right away, right here and now.

11
00:01:07,706 --> 00:01:19,056
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's that... it's that pressing need, impatient need of... of removing it as soon as it arises or as soon as it starts arising.

12
00:01:19,756 --> 00:01:22,799
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why it makes it so... much more unpleasant.

13
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:35,950
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you stop trying to get rid of it, then you can... you can... well, you can be able to... to see it closer, to see it for what it is.

14
00:01:36,478 --> 00:01:44,802
[SPEAKER_01]: And what it is, is that it's not an acute issue or a problem that has arisen as a kind of mistake.

15
00:01:45,683 --> 00:02:05,913
[SPEAKER_01]: It's really mirroring of a very basic, very primordial existential principle, existential discrepancy, if you want to call it like that, which is that this life of mine, my own life,

16
00:02:08,029 --> 00:02:20,275
[SPEAKER_01]: My own environment, it's not my own, in a sense of fundamentally, things upon which my life rests, things that determine my life, are not in my control.

17
00:02:21,836 --> 00:02:34,403
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why anxiety, actually, far from being like an acute problem or some error in your programming, it's really just

18
00:02:35,827 --> 00:02:42,792
[SPEAKER_01]: Just a revelation of the... of the most certain thing, when it comes down to your existence.

19
00:02:42,892 --> 00:02:46,334
[SPEAKER_01]: And that thing is... it's... your own existence is not in your control.

20
00:02:47,615 --> 00:02:56,881
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't mean that your choices are not in your control, but means that choices are already within that existence, that you have no say in it.

21
00:02:57,321 --> 00:02:58,202
[SPEAKER_01]: You have no say in...

22
00:03:01,241 --> 00:03:06,123
[SPEAKER_01]: In the fundamental aspects of your environment, you are not safe in the circumstances that can affect your life.

23
00:03:06,884 --> 00:03:11,626
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only do the best you can within that limited amount of control.

24
00:03:12,886 --> 00:03:24,852
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you look at it closely, fundamentally, no amount of control can ever change or upturn that order and truly make you the master of your own experience, of your own life.

25
00:03:25,292 --> 00:03:25,492
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

26
00:03:25,532 --> 00:03:26,573
[SPEAKER_01]: Because fundamentally,

27
00:03:27,670 --> 00:03:47,953
[SPEAKER_01]: The fact that you're going to be subjected to elements, to change, adverse change or positive change, the fact that that remains there as something you're fundamentally and utterly subjected to, that's exactly what anxiety reveals.

28
00:03:48,014 --> 00:03:55,435
[SPEAKER_01]: Reveals that... reveals the discrepancy between your assumption of your world and the actual nature of it.

29
00:03:56,155 --> 00:03:56,695
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the

30
00:03:57,313 --> 00:03:59,094
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why anxiety is unpleasant.

31
00:03:59,555 --> 00:04:20,552
[SPEAKER_01]: If you were to remove the discrepancy, if you were to remove the view that believes that you are the master control of your feelings, for example, that would basically remove the unpleasant aspect of anxiety, and then anxiety would not be anxiety as you know it,

32
00:04:21,187 --> 00:04:27,610
[SPEAKER_01]: It would simply be a recognition of the fundamental principle of life, which is, it is not in your control.

33
00:04:28,411 --> 00:04:30,252
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot be fundamentally yours.

34
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:38,076
[SPEAKER_01]: By that, I mean, you cannot be the owner, because if you were truly the owner, the life, the feelings would obey you.

35
00:04:40,317 --> 00:04:41,898
[SPEAKER_01]: You would feel only what you want to feel.

36
00:04:43,299 --> 00:04:45,380
[SPEAKER_01]: You would experience only what you want to experience.

37
00:04:47,081 --> 00:04:49,762
[SPEAKER_01]: But the fact that that that's simply not possible,

38
00:04:50,284 --> 00:04:54,507
[SPEAKER_01]: You end up living your life at odds with the very nature of it.

39
00:04:56,009 --> 00:05:02,934
[SPEAKER_01]: Your attitude towards your own feelings, pleasure, displeasure, neutral feelings, is at odds with the actual nature of those feelings.

40
00:05:03,975 --> 00:05:05,076
[SPEAKER_01]: They arise on their own.

41
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:07,698
[SPEAKER_01]: They manifest themselves to you.

42
00:05:09,019 --> 00:05:10,861
[SPEAKER_01]: And the problem... that's where the problem arises.

43
00:05:11,041 --> 00:05:17,306
[SPEAKER_01]: Whereby, when pleasant feelings manifest themselves to you, you want them and you feel fully entitled in doing so.

44
00:05:17,766 --> 00:05:19,668
[SPEAKER_01]: You feel fully entitled in going after them.

45
00:05:20,730 --> 00:05:27,455
[SPEAKER_01]: You feel fully entitled in entertaining them, building your decisions, your choices upon them, and so on.

46
00:05:28,956 --> 00:05:35,461
[SPEAKER_01]: But now, when you have a disagreeable feeling arises, you equally feel fully entitled to try to get rid of it right away.

47
00:05:36,982 --> 00:05:37,922
[SPEAKER_01]: I must not be feeling this.

48
00:05:38,042 --> 00:05:39,584
[SPEAKER_01]: I should not be feeling this.

49
00:05:40,324 --> 00:05:41,025
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what I mean.

50
00:05:41,465 --> 00:05:49,911
[SPEAKER_01]: In order to... like such a kind of subtle, overwhelming, yet so general experience of arisen anxiety, unpleasant anxiety,

51
00:05:50,376 --> 00:05:54,697
[SPEAKER_01]: The first thing is to stop acting out of that sense of, I have a right to not want this.

52
00:05:56,097 --> 00:06:07,820
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever has a reason, it has a reason on its own, be it this feeling or that feeling, which means, eh... your rights stop there, so to speak.

53
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,221
[SPEAKER_01]: You have a right to choose like this or to choose like that.

54
00:06:11,361 --> 00:06:19,643
[SPEAKER_01]: You have a right to take responsibility for your choices, but you have a no... you don't have a right to not feel this or... because whatever is being felt,

55
00:06:20,783 --> 00:06:24,224
[SPEAKER_01]: It's felt on the basis of this life that's subjected to feelings.

56
00:06:25,964 --> 00:06:30,885
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why it's... it's really... the anxiety is really not about freeing yourself from the unpleasant feeling.

57
00:06:31,245 --> 00:06:41,347
[SPEAKER_01]: It's freeing yourself from the view that you yourself impose upon the very present experience that you have at a time, that then results in this discrepancy.

58
00:06:42,048 --> 00:06:45,948
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you... and... and you can't get rid of a view, whatever the view is, overnight.

59
00:06:46,369 --> 00:06:47,189
[SPEAKER_01]: It won't happen so.

60
00:06:47,709 --> 00:06:48,309
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can't...

61
00:06:49,076 --> 00:06:53,197
[SPEAKER_01]: Just suddenly shift your view and be free from everything that bothers you.

62
00:06:53,877 --> 00:07:00,719
[SPEAKER_01]: View is... it's... it's really like a... like a... like a habit, like a habit of a certain way of perceiving things.

63
00:07:01,139 --> 00:07:05,240
[SPEAKER_01]: So, now you need to reprogram the way you perceive things.

64
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:14,322
[SPEAKER_01]: And you reprogram it when you start following the principles for reprogramming, not just when you want to act out of it, when things are only unpleasant.

65
00:07:14,522 --> 00:07:15,403
[SPEAKER_01]: Now I want to do it.

66
00:07:15,963 --> 00:07:17,263
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, when anxiety is gone,

67
00:07:17,792 --> 00:07:21,433
[SPEAKER_01]: You forget about it and you pretend like it was never there and your life is fine.

68
00:07:21,673 --> 00:07:24,094
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no such thing as fine life.

69
00:07:24,114 --> 00:07:28,115
[SPEAKER_01]: As in, there is no such thing as life free from anxiety or suffering.

70
00:07:30,095 --> 00:07:34,717
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no such thing as as life that doesn't require taking up responsibility.

71
00:07:36,477 --> 00:07:39,298
[SPEAKER_01]: That doesn't require work.

72
00:07:39,318 --> 00:07:40,998
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's really not... that's not optional.

73
00:07:41,038 --> 00:07:43,119
[SPEAKER_01]: What is optional is how you're going to go about it.

74
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:53,243
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you going to be trying to mask the fact that anxiety reveals you the most fundamental nature of your existence, that you're not in your control, that your life is not in your control?

75
00:07:53,283 --> 00:08:01,328
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, mask it, pretend it's not there, distract yourself with with sensual pleasures, or are you going to start accepting responsibility for it and start looking at it?

76
00:08:02,869 --> 00:08:07,713
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... if it's... sometimes it might feel overwhelming and unpleasant,

77
00:08:09,393 --> 00:08:17,438
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's pretty much because most of the habits are still concerned about running away from it and not accepting it.

78
00:08:18,659 --> 00:08:20,540
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's going to take time to be able to accept it.

79
00:08:21,281 --> 00:08:29,166
[SPEAKER_01]: And once you accept it, then you, as I said, then you realize, well, the unpleasant aspect of anxiety, it's not necessary.

80
00:08:29,866 --> 00:08:37,932
[SPEAKER_01]: Anxiety in itself, as a revelation of of that discrepancy that your life is, the way it's lived, that is absolutely fine.

81
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:39,334
[SPEAKER_01]: That's just how it is.

82
00:08:39,835 --> 00:08:43,956
[SPEAKER_01]: You remove the discrepancy, you remove that displeasure of that anxiety.

83
00:08:45,217 --> 00:09:01,584
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if, eh... it's... if a person... it would be good, starting point, to... to sort of, eh... stop expecting an override solution, stop resisting trying to get rid of it.

84
00:09:02,804 --> 00:09:04,085
[SPEAKER_01]: That's probably the most important.

85
00:09:05,626 --> 00:09:21,938
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you, you know, when you have thoughts, oh, how great things would be without this, without this anxiety, you can use that as a motivation to make the effort to understand anxiety, but don't use that as a justification to want to get rid of it.

86
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:31,245
[SPEAKER_01]: Because the notions you have of, oh, how great it would be of being anxiety-free, are really a fantasy.

87
00:09:31,285 --> 00:09:34,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, if the life was in your control,

88
00:09:34,897 --> 00:09:40,662
[SPEAKER_01]: If the life was the way you think it is, anxiety would be inconceivable.

89
00:09:41,703 --> 00:09:48,188
[SPEAKER_01]: But the fact that it isn't, the fact that it has arisen, the fact that you're experiencing it, means now you have an option.

90
00:09:48,208 --> 00:09:58,016
[SPEAKER_01]: You're either going to pretend that that's a mistake, or you're going to start looking into your own attitude towards your own life and realize that that's the bit that needs changing.

91
00:09:58,977 --> 00:10:01,919
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, as I said, anxiety is a symptom, it's not a problem.

92
00:10:03,291 --> 00:10:08,612
[SPEAKER_01]: It reveals the discrepancy that you yourself generate and maintain with your attitude towards your own existence.

93
00:10:10,513 --> 00:10:13,594
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not the problem of your existence.

94
00:10:13,634 --> 00:10:15,854
[SPEAKER_01]: Existence itself is not a problem.

95
00:10:15,874 --> 00:10:20,815
[SPEAKER_01]: The problem arises when there is a discrepancy, when there is a certain disparity.

96
00:10:20,955 --> 00:10:22,876
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what normal is.

97
00:10:22,936 --> 00:10:28,417
[SPEAKER_01]: Normal life is the life based upon that disparity, contradiction.

98
00:10:29,718 --> 00:10:31,198
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why normal life requires

99
00:10:31,618 --> 00:10:34,159
[SPEAKER_01]: That constant sort of engagement and maintenance.

100
00:10:34,179 --> 00:10:35,760
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people are afraid of solitude.

101
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:38,261
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people are superstitious.

102
00:10:38,361 --> 00:10:50,027
[SPEAKER_01]: All these little... like fear of solitude, for example, just starts pointing you back towards that which you're running away from with your daily distractions and actions and projects and meanings and so on.

103
00:10:50,527 --> 00:10:52,328
[SPEAKER_01]: When you're alone, you're just left with your own thoughts.

104
00:10:52,348 --> 00:10:53,749
[SPEAKER_01]: And what's going to show itself first?

105
00:10:54,189 --> 00:10:56,650
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, first is going to be boredom, then it's going to be dread and anxiety.

106
00:10:57,651 --> 00:10:59,652
[SPEAKER_01]: Because your whole life is about covering it up.

107
00:11:00,275 --> 00:11:04,477
[SPEAKER_01]: And that needs constant kind of floating, constant swimming on the surface.

108
00:11:05,257 --> 00:11:06,257
[SPEAKER_00]: Superstition, same.

109
00:11:07,198 --> 00:11:13,780
[SPEAKER_01]: People develop magical beliefs to mask that little crack in their existence where anxiety shows its head through.

110
00:11:15,401 --> 00:11:23,044
[SPEAKER_01]: But again, if existence were perfect, if existence is the way you would think it is, none of these things would be conceivable.

111
00:11:23,965 --> 00:11:28,166
[SPEAKER_01]: Anxiety, displeasure for that matter, would be absolutely inconceivable.

112
00:11:28,947 --> 00:11:29,807
[SPEAKER_00]: You could not think it.

113
00:11:31,406 --> 00:11:31,526
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

114
00:11:31,586 --> 00:11:42,868
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you would be the master controller and things would be corresponding to that mastery, your choices, your feelings, your intentions, which means there would be no discrepancy to be felt as displeasure.

115
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:49,429
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's... it really comes down to... down to changing your view in regard to your own existence.

116
00:11:51,050 --> 00:11:51,690
[SPEAKER_01]: Upgrading it.

117
00:11:52,590 --> 00:11:53,610
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it is an upgrade.

118
00:11:58,371 --> 00:11:58,631
[SPEAKER_01]: Once the

119
00:11:59,147 --> 00:12:13,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you become aware of the problem, once you become aware of the anxiety, eh... means you become aware, obviously, unwillingly, of the fundamental aspect of your own life.

120
00:12:16,239 --> 00:12:26,005
[SPEAKER_01]: An aspect that's very unpleasant, not in itself, but it's unpleasant because of your own assumptions in regard to your own life that are at odds with it.

121
00:12:27,306 --> 00:12:28,787
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop trying to get rid of the anxiety,

122
00:12:29,436 --> 00:12:30,216
[SPEAKER_01]: This is the first step.

123
00:12:30,757 --> 00:12:45,063
[SPEAKER_01]: The second step is you have to start looking at it as a symptom, not as a problem, not as something I must deal with it, but something that has an underlying cause that's being revealed to me through that anxiety.

124
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:53,447
[SPEAKER_01]: And that underlying cause is that... is the very nature of your life, of your feelings, of things you're subjected to.

125
00:12:55,885 --> 00:13:02,130
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is at odds with what you think those things are, or what you feel those things should be.

126
00:13:02,150 --> 00:13:09,977
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's... that's why, like, naturally, that view, that assumption, carries already a sense of entitlement.

127
00:13:10,117 --> 00:13:21,147
[SPEAKER_01]: But... but for that assumption, you're responsible, simply because you don't dwell on that nature... of that underlying nature of that... of that experience.

128
00:13:21,247 --> 00:13:22,648
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't... you don't dwell enough

129
00:13:23,392 --> 00:13:31,115
[SPEAKER_01]: On the fact that you are not in your control, you don't dwell enough on the fact that feelings arise on their own and you're subjected to them.

130
00:13:32,176 --> 00:13:42,760
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you can... you can act out of them, you could try to cover them up, but fundamentally, you can never uproot your liability to feel good, bad or neutral.

131
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:43,540
[SPEAKER_01]: You just can't.

132
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:46,101
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your efforts are only secondary.

133
00:13:47,562 --> 00:13:50,443
[SPEAKER_01]: The amount of input you can... you can make, it's only relative.

134
00:13:51,607 --> 00:13:53,608
[SPEAKER_01]: It cannot fundamentally upturn that picture.

135
00:13:54,028 --> 00:14:18,480
[SPEAKER_01]: But see, not thinking about these things, feeling entitled to not think about these things, and then feeling even further entitlement towards sensuality and pleasures and craving and ambition in life and trying to get your desires fulfilled, that's how you proliferate that very discrepancy between how things actually are and how you think they should be.

136
00:14:19,447 --> 00:14:21,989
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly... that's exactly where anxiety is.

137
00:14:23,170 --> 00:14:33,278
[SPEAKER_01]: So, removal of your expectation how things should be, learning how to accept the way things are, and that's something, as I said, you're not done... do it in a second.

138
00:14:33,878 --> 00:14:36,400
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to... you have to keep drilling it.

139
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:42,225
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to keep training yourself in regard to it, because you really... you're not just dealing with one particular problem.

140
00:14:42,905 --> 00:14:46,548
[SPEAKER_01]: You're... you're re... reprogramming the entire

141
00:14:47,402 --> 00:14:49,443
[SPEAKER_01]: Attitude towards your own existence that you have.

142
00:14:49,623 --> 00:14:56,306
[SPEAKER_01]: And reprogramming takes time, takes repetition, eh... until you undo the the wrong programming habits.

143
00:14:57,406 --> 00:15:00,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Habits of trying to get rid of the unpleasant feelings as soon as they're manifested.

144
00:15:01,248 --> 00:15:05,530
[SPEAKER_01]: Habits of trying to to to run away from the unpleasant feelings as soon as they're manifested.

145
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:08,391
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's also another thing you can think about.

146
00:15:08,471 --> 00:15:13,733
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is unpleasant feeling, be it anxiety or anything else, why is it my problem?

147
00:15:14,633 --> 00:15:15,714
[SPEAKER_01]: The anxiety arises,

148
00:15:17,689 --> 00:15:19,049
[SPEAKER_01]: It's felt unpleasantly.

149
00:15:19,730 --> 00:15:20,890
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is that an issue?

150
00:15:21,910 --> 00:15:23,531
[SPEAKER_01]: Why immediately I must get rid of this?

151
00:15:24,411 --> 00:15:24,571
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

152
00:15:24,771 --> 00:15:25,131
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know.

153
00:15:25,151 --> 00:15:31,393
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, I'm still fully aware and fully responsible for my actions, so I don't need to choose or decide to do anything on account of it.

154
00:15:32,033 --> 00:15:33,553
[SPEAKER_01]: Why I cannot just be with it?

155
00:15:35,114 --> 00:15:36,774
[SPEAKER_01]: Something worth dwelling on.

156
00:15:37,574 --> 00:15:44,176
[SPEAKER_01]: And equally, when pleasant feelings, when enticing sort of perceptions manifest themselves and you want that pleasure,

157
00:15:45,053 --> 00:15:47,935
[SPEAKER_01]: Ask yourself, why do I have to follow this desire?

158
00:15:48,915 --> 00:15:52,057
[SPEAKER_01]: Why I cannot just remain equanimous towards it?

159
00:15:54,178 --> 00:15:55,899
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, it doesn't...

160
00:15:56,239 --> 00:16:03,903
[SPEAKER_01]: Neither desire for sensuality, nor anxiety and unpleasant feeling, neither of those things makes you act.

161
00:16:04,644 --> 00:16:07,085
[SPEAKER_01]: You are the one who chooses to act upon it.

162
00:16:08,645 --> 00:16:15,089
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, they can exert different pressure, and that different pressure means different amount of discrepancy, and that depends on where your views are at.

163
00:16:16,049 --> 00:16:21,732
[SPEAKER_01]: The more you feel entitled to sensuality, the more pressure is going to exhibit on you.

164
00:16:21,792 --> 00:16:28,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Same, the more entitled you feel to be free from any unpleasant feeling, the more frightening anxiety will be.

165
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:38,161
[SPEAKER_01]: But, again, doesn't doesn't matter how much fear or how much pressure towards sensual pleasure and desire is manifested,

166
00:16:38,922 --> 00:16:44,065
[SPEAKER_01]: You are the one, fundamentally and ultimately, who decides to act or not out of it.

167
00:16:44,945 --> 00:16:46,446
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's where your responsibility is.

168
00:16:46,986 --> 00:16:48,747
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize, I don't have to act out of this.

169
00:16:49,187 --> 00:16:50,108
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't have to do anything.

170
00:16:50,868 --> 00:16:53,149
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't have to do anything on account of there is an anxiety.

171
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:55,951
[SPEAKER_01]: I could just patiently allow it to endure.

172
00:16:57,071 --> 00:16:59,913
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, the mind will go, I must get rid of it, I must get rid of it.

173
00:17:00,013 --> 00:17:02,234
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'll endure that thought as well.

174
00:17:02,654 --> 00:17:04,155
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll endure those states of mind.

175
00:17:05,096 --> 00:17:05,356
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

176
00:17:05,776 --> 00:17:07,757
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, fundamentally, as I said,

177
00:17:08,639 --> 00:17:14,743
[SPEAKER_01]: Anxiety is not the issue that accidentally erroneously arose on account of your perfect existence.

178
00:17:15,704 --> 00:17:21,788
[SPEAKER_01]: Anxiety is an issue that reveals to you that existence, in its nature, is imperfect.

179
00:17:22,769 --> 00:17:27,413
[SPEAKER_01]: But the imperfection, it's not in existence, it's in your attitude toward your own existence.

180
00:17:28,914 --> 00:17:35,238
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why, that's why really, anxiety, it's almost like an existential awakening.

181
00:17:36,819 --> 00:17:37,700
[SPEAKER_01]: Because most people,

182
00:17:38,916 --> 00:17:40,117
[SPEAKER_01]: Everybody experiences anxiety.

183
00:17:40,157 --> 00:17:41,578
[SPEAKER_01]: There's absolutely... that's not optional.

184
00:17:42,119 --> 00:17:48,543
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's... that's the first thing that's going to become apparent if you start accepting it as a symptom of your resistance, not as an issue.

185
00:17:48,563 --> 00:17:51,165
[SPEAKER_01]: You'll see that everybody, everybody is subjected to it.

186
00:17:51,826 --> 00:18:02,254
[SPEAKER_01]: But the difference is that most people are still able to maintain that... that... that thin layer of ignorance, very frail layer of ignorance upon it.

187
00:18:04,476 --> 00:18:06,077
[SPEAKER_01]: So they... they can pretend it's not there.

188
00:18:06,784 --> 00:18:07,564
[SPEAKER_01]: But it is.

189
00:18:07,664 --> 00:18:15,025
[SPEAKER_01]: It's always there, it always has been, always will be, for as long as the view toward your existence is at odds with the existence.

190
00:18:15,826 --> 00:18:22,107
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's always there, but some people are still able to keep distracting themselves from it.

191
00:18:22,147 --> 00:18:24,087
[SPEAKER_01]: But that doesn't mean they're dealing with it.

192
00:18:24,847 --> 00:18:26,627
[SPEAKER_01]: It actually... it makes things worse.

193
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:35,689
[SPEAKER_01]: The more you're distracting yourself from it, the more of that discrepancy, the habit that results in the discrepancy, is being reinforced.

194
00:18:36,673 --> 00:18:41,256
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you spend your whole life running away from anxiety, ultimately, it catches up with you.

195
00:18:41,396 --> 00:18:43,637
[SPEAKER_01]: When death comes, how do you think it's going to feel?

196
00:18:44,177 --> 00:18:53,323
[SPEAKER_01]: If little... either public speaking or other things cause you anxiety, how do you think, when your life starts to shut down, how that's going to feel?

197
00:18:54,263 --> 00:18:59,426
[SPEAKER_01]: When little threats to your existence, secondary threats to your existence, make you anxious.

198
00:18:59,446 --> 00:19:03,008
[SPEAKER_01]: Imagine when that threat is actually being realized and you are done.

199
00:19:03,028 --> 00:19:04,529
[SPEAKER_01]: For whatever reason, it doesn't matter what

200
00:19:06,288 --> 00:19:10,410
[SPEAKER_01]: What brings death on, the point is, that's what anxiety is.

201
00:19:10,590 --> 00:19:11,770
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what anxiety shows you.

202
00:19:12,150 --> 00:19:16,012
[SPEAKER_01]: That your life can end at any given time, and you have no say in that.

203
00:19:16,392 --> 00:19:19,053
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, you live your life as if you have a say in that.

204
00:19:20,274 --> 00:19:28,017
[SPEAKER_01]: Your health can end at any given time, yet you're fully intoxicated with the fact that you're not ill now, and you think you're never gonna get ill.

205
00:19:28,517 --> 00:19:30,958
[SPEAKER_01]: Same with youth, strength and age.

206
00:19:31,972 --> 00:19:40,039
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why those three divine messengers that the Buddha himself was talking about, sickness, aging and death, are the, like, messengers.

207
00:19:40,299 --> 00:19:42,661
[SPEAKER_01]: They are the symptoms of the problem.

208
00:19:42,941 --> 00:19:43,642
[SPEAKER_01]: They are not the problem.

209
00:19:43,662 --> 00:19:45,423
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize, this is inevitable.

210
00:19:46,164 --> 00:19:58,674
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I better tailor my views, my attitude towards my existence to match this, so that there is no discrepancy affecting me, destroying me and really, really making me suffer when it comes.

211
00:20:00,572 --> 00:20:15,495
[SPEAKER_01]: So, trying to... trying to not get rid of it, accepting it, and then developing an attitude towards your own anxiety as a symptom of an underlying problem, not an issue in itself.

212
00:20:16,895 --> 00:20:29,058
[SPEAKER_01]: And, in order to approve the issue that anxiety is a symptom of, you have to start... well, you have to start modifying your own life and your own views towards it.

213
00:20:29,553 --> 00:20:37,199
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you feel like, oh, it's too much work, look at all these happy people around me, that's your own mind sort of playing tricks on you, in a sense of...

214
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,161
[SPEAKER_01]: In a way, it's a lazy thinking.

215
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:43,724
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't want to do work, look how all these people are happy, I just want to be like that, I just want this to go away.

216
00:20:44,105 --> 00:20:45,626
[SPEAKER_01]: That is wishful thinking.

217
00:20:45,666 --> 00:20:57,095
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can carry on wishing that, and the more you wish it, the more you'll be subjected to that discrepancy, or you could take up responsibility for it, and realize, no, this is something worth addressing.

218
00:20:57,673 --> 00:21:00,935
[SPEAKER_01]: Something worth dealing, because it's not something you need to do every time.

219
00:21:01,215 --> 00:21:03,737
[SPEAKER_01]: If you truly, properly address it and deal with it, that's it.

220
00:21:04,257 --> 00:21:06,118
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no discrepancy to be felt anymore.

221
00:21:06,138 --> 00:21:07,059
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a true freedom.

222
00:21:07,619 --> 00:21:11,541
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no pressure of... of sense desires that you can or cannot fulfill.

223
00:21:11,561 --> 00:21:13,242
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no fear of, oh, what if this happen?

224
00:21:13,262 --> 00:21:13,963
[SPEAKER_01]: What if that happen?

225
00:21:14,863 --> 00:21:15,904
[SPEAKER_01]: There are still those thoughts.

226
00:21:15,944 --> 00:21:16,644
[SPEAKER_01]: What if this happen?

227
00:21:16,664 --> 00:21:17,285
[SPEAKER_01]: What if that happen?

228
00:21:17,725 --> 00:21:22,628
[SPEAKER_01]: But those thoughts are now not causing any discrepancy, because you have no expectations.

229
00:21:23,393 --> 00:21:28,297
[SPEAKER_01]: Certainly not assumed fixed expectations as to or this must happen or this should happen.

230
00:21:30,058 --> 00:21:37,343
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in that sense, anxiety is still there, but now you are not there with it anymore.

231
00:21:37,463 --> 00:21:38,244
[SPEAKER_01]: You went beyond it.

232
00:21:38,764 --> 00:21:41,626
[SPEAKER_01]: The reason it bothers you is because it threatens to overwhelm you.

233
00:21:42,187 --> 00:21:46,190
[SPEAKER_01]: But it threatens to overwhelm you because you're too weak in regard to it.

234
00:21:47,150 --> 00:21:52,154
[SPEAKER_01]: And you're too weak in regard to it because you never want to take responsibility for developing strength towards it.

235
00:21:53,773 --> 00:22:11,747
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you do so, and you make that effort of being able to allow it to endure, not carelessly acting out of a habit, trying to get rid of it, not carelessly trying to distract yourself from it through sensuality and desire, then you'll see it coming and going, yet your mind composure will remain unchanged.

236
00:22:12,407 --> 00:22:19,933
[SPEAKER_01]: And that is a true freedom, when you are not liable to the pressure of your own feelings, whenever they arise, whatever they might be as well.

237
00:22:20,587 --> 00:22:23,488
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when there is pleasure, you're not trying to get more of it automatically.

238
00:22:23,528 --> 00:22:25,888
[SPEAKER_01]: When there's pain, you're not trying to get rid of it automatically.

239
00:22:27,008 --> 00:22:30,609
[SPEAKER_01]: And when there's neither pleasure nor pain, you're not distracted automatically.

240
00:22:32,109 --> 00:22:33,849
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the feeling arise and endure.

241
00:22:34,989 --> 00:22:43,051
[SPEAKER_01]: But the mind state, the composure of your mind, remains completely unaffected by that.

242
00:22:43,771 --> 00:22:49,532
[SPEAKER_01]: This should also answer the question whether there is some technique, meditation technique you can do

243
00:22:50,584 --> 00:23:05,918
[SPEAKER_01]: In order to overcome anxiety, eh... that question, as it should be, well, clearer from this by now, would be coming from the... that... that view that I should be getting rid of this, that I should not feel anxiety in the first place.

244
00:23:07,119 --> 00:23:17,208
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... so... so... so once you... once you stop having such expectations, you realize there is no prescription method

245
00:23:17,709 --> 00:23:18,470
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no such thing.

246
00:23:18,490 --> 00:23:19,910
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is why, again, we go back to the same.

247
00:23:19,930 --> 00:23:24,613
[SPEAKER_01]: The most important thing you can do, in regard to the experience of anxiety, is swallow the hard pill of truth, in a sense, so that you realize

248
00:23:46,150 --> 00:23:48,391
[SPEAKER_01]: It really shows you what existence is about.

249
00:23:49,872 --> 00:23:57,075
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not something that can be ignored and then you can pretend that it was never there and continue your life merrily and ignorantly.

250
00:23:58,456 --> 00:24:06,440
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you if you're able to accept that as a truth, that's already a massive step forward in order to be able to not be affected by anxiety.

251
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:07,701
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't get rid of it.

252
00:24:07,741 --> 00:24:10,022
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, you can't get rid of your own existence.

253
00:24:10,382 --> 00:24:14,404
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only grow out of that anxiety, whereby when it arises,

254
00:24:15,110 --> 00:24:16,370
[SPEAKER_01]: You are not affected by it.

255
00:24:17,991 --> 00:24:24,853
[SPEAKER_01]: And the only way you'll stop being affected by it, is if you stop running away from it, which keeps giving it power.

256
00:24:26,174 --> 00:24:36,697
[SPEAKER_01]: So, a symptom that tells you, that reveals the underlying nature of your existence, well, it's not what you want to be.

257
00:24:36,717 --> 00:24:40,038
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not what you assume to be.

258
00:24:40,118 --> 00:24:42,019
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're willing to accept it as such,

259
00:24:42,917 --> 00:24:46,240
[SPEAKER_01]: It's already like less than half of a problem.

260
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:55,246
[SPEAKER_01]: The main problem is people still maintaining the prior or the notions prior to the anxiety.

261
00:24:55,446 --> 00:24:56,887
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, not prior to anxiety.

262
00:24:56,987 --> 00:24:58,348
[SPEAKER_01]: You're always subject to anxiety.

263
00:24:58,829 --> 00:25:01,871
[SPEAKER_01]: Prior to their anxiety, becoming self-aware.

264
00:25:03,112 --> 00:25:05,954
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you think there was the norm before that.

265
00:25:06,094 --> 00:25:06,675
[SPEAKER_01]: But it isn't.

266
00:25:06,855 --> 00:25:08,616
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, if there were truly the norm,

267
00:25:09,411 --> 00:25:19,656
[SPEAKER_01]: Anxiety would have not arisen in the first place, because if you were truly the master, controller of your feelings, of your environment, of your life, you would feel only what you want to feel.

268
00:25:20,756 --> 00:25:23,478
[SPEAKER_01]: And the Buddha himself spoke about it many times.

269
00:25:23,498 --> 00:25:29,541
[SPEAKER_01]: He says, which feeling is yours, as in which feeling you think you control, because they keep changing.

270
00:25:31,301 --> 00:25:36,364
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you were truly the controller, you would only feel what you want to feel.

271
00:25:36,384 --> 00:25:38,925
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can apply the same principle towards your own thoughts.

272
00:25:39,806 --> 00:25:43,687
[SPEAKER_01]: If you were truly the controller of your thoughts, you would only think what you want to think.

273
00:25:45,048 --> 00:25:45,368
[SPEAKER_01]: But no.

274
00:25:45,488 --> 00:25:52,390
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts manifest themselves, they present themselves to you, and then you make choices and decisions and think further based upon that.

275
00:25:52,610 --> 00:25:54,891
[SPEAKER_01]: But fundamentally, they were arisen on their own.

276
00:25:55,851 --> 00:25:59,793
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why they did fundamental, ultimate responsibility for your actions.

277
00:26:00,373 --> 00:26:04,434
[SPEAKER_01]: No amount of thoughts arising on their own, no amount of feelings pressuring you on their own.

278
00:26:05,735 --> 00:26:07,335
[SPEAKER_01]: None of that can make you act.

279
00:26:07,655 --> 00:26:09,496
[SPEAKER_01]: Only you choosing to act

280
00:26:10,172 --> 00:26:10,932
[SPEAKER_01]: Makes you act.

281
00:26:12,193 --> 00:26:13,994
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what you're fully responsible for.

282
00:26:14,254 --> 00:26:15,375
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is an excuse for that.

283
00:26:15,735 --> 00:26:24,240
[SPEAKER_01]: Because none of the feelings, none of the thoughts, none of the... even the intentions that present themselves, none of them automatically result in this action or that, oh, I've done this because of that.

284
00:26:24,420 --> 00:26:24,560
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

285
00:26:25,201 --> 00:26:28,903
[SPEAKER_01]: You've done this because you chose that to be the reason for doing this.

286
00:26:31,164 --> 00:26:33,726
[SPEAKER_01]: And and that's... that's simply... there's no alternative to this.

287
00:26:36,127 --> 00:26:38,909
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why that acceptance of

288
00:26:39,341 --> 00:26:43,442
[SPEAKER_01]: What you're subjected to, in terms of feeling, in terms of thoughts, in terms of the environment.

289
00:26:44,022 --> 00:26:45,703
[SPEAKER_01]: Acceptance, in a sense, not...

290
00:26:45,723 --> 00:26:46,523
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, I don't...

291
00:26:46,563 --> 00:26:48,324
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't do anything about it.

292
00:26:48,364 --> 00:27:01,148
[SPEAKER_01]: Acceptance, in a sense, I must not try to get rid of this, but instead, I have to look where the real problem is, which is in the discrepancy that I create in regard to things that I'm subjected to.

293
00:27:01,168 --> 00:27:08,510
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, I mean, if... if... if certain type of environment, it's causing you overwhelming anxiety, sure.

294
00:27:09,197 --> 00:27:10,017
[SPEAKER_01]: Turn it down a bit.

295
00:27:10,538 --> 00:27:11,578
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't expose yourself to it.

296
00:27:11,778 --> 00:27:15,000
[SPEAKER_01]: But not for the sake of sheltering yourself from anxiety.

297
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:21,223
[SPEAKER_01]: Just for the sake of giving yourself a bit of a break, so that you can regain strength to deal with it.

298
00:27:23,164 --> 00:27:26,505
[SPEAKER_01]: And you don't deal with it by going straight into what makes you anxious.

299
00:27:26,525 --> 00:27:27,566
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

300
00:27:27,666 --> 00:27:38,291
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, you deal with it by changing, upgrading, reprogramming your views about that thing that causes you anxiety, or about life in general.

301
00:27:39,197 --> 00:27:52,544
[SPEAKER_01]: Your expectations, your entitlement, your assumptions, if you get that to match the actual nature of existence, the actual nature of your life, then there will be no discrepancy.

302
00:27:52,624 --> 00:28:03,829
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the less disparity between the two, the less liability to anxiety, the less amount of symptoms will be showing.

303
00:28:07,797 --> 00:28:09,017
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why, that's what I mean.

304
00:28:09,098 --> 00:28:13,799
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a gradual work, gradual effort, gradual acceptance, in a way, and gradual reprogramming.

305
00:28:15,200 --> 00:28:24,443
[SPEAKER_01]: And you can only, only do so, not based out of a, out of a, out of a mechanical kind of sets of observances and rules, and I do this, and I do this.

306
00:28:24,523 --> 00:28:24,703
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

307
00:28:24,783 --> 00:28:26,724
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only do so by reflecting upon it.

308
00:28:27,865 --> 00:28:31,986
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can only do so by accepting the fearful aspect of it, bit by bit.

309
00:28:32,406 --> 00:28:34,667
[SPEAKER_01]: But you realize, that's the work that needs to be done.

310
00:28:35,087 --> 00:28:37,208
[SPEAKER_01]: Not, that's the work that I must get rid of.

311
00:28:38,728 --> 00:28:41,369
[SPEAKER_01]: It's done when it doesn't affect you.

312
00:28:41,389 --> 00:28:43,570
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not done when it's just not there.

313
00:28:45,211 --> 00:28:54,436
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, as I said, anxiety mirrors the nature of existence, which means, in a way, that mirror is always there.

314
00:28:54,456 --> 00:28:56,757
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just whether you're going to suffer on account of it or not.

